[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-b952ad6f-218a-4819-ac62-b59d8d5594cd\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Wed 15 Apr 2026 16:15 - 16:30 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2026/icse-2026-venue-oceania-x\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Oceania X</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Dependability and Security 3</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/larsgrunske\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Lars Grunske</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"b952ad6f-218a-4819-ac62-b59d8d5594cd\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>AnchorDiff: Binary OSS Version Identification Method Based on Anchor Node Slicing</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Virtual Attendance\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Virtual Attendance\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/5a83481a-76b0-4d52-a281-ed633e8995d2/small?1776349051000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><p>Binary Open-Source Software (OSS) is commonly embedded as third-party code within firmware and downstream software architectures, for simplifying the development process.<br>\nHowever, vulnerabilities existing in OSS can be propagated through code reuse into embedded firmware and software architectures, posing security risks to these devices.<br>\nTo mitigate the security risks in firmware and software architectures, researchers have identified the versions of extracted firmware or binary software to detect N-day vulnerabilities in OSS.<br>\nExisting works have achieved several success, but new challenges of non-linear update and minor updates hinder the improvement of the accuracy of binary OSS version identification.</p>\n<p>In this paper, we propose AnchorDiff, an efficient and accurate framework of binary OSS version identification.<br>\nAnchorDiff filters out versions with significant updates from all OSS versions as <em>Anchor Nodes</em> which serve as boundaries to partition the entire version chain into sub-regions.<br>\nThe target file\u2019s sub-region is located based on the binary code similarity detection (BCSD) results with the <em>Anchor Nodes</em>\u2019 function libraries.<br>\nFinally, AnchorDiff uses the Adaptive Weight Fine-grained Matching (AWM) algorithm to weight the fine-grained matching results and determine the true version of the target binary file.</p>\n<p>The experimental results show that AnchorDiff achieves the best performance in identifying binary OSS versions with complex compilation configurations in both small and large OSS datasets, with accuracies reaching 90.35% and 97.17% respectively, which are 2.76% and 20.99% higher than the current state-of-the-art (SOTA) work.<br>\nIn terms of database storage, AnchorDiff reduces storage requirements by a factor of 36, compared to the original binary files.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/zixuanliang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zixuan Liang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">National University of Defense Technology</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/leizhou\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Lei Zhou<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">National University of Defense Technology</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/yongqiangguo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yongqiang Guo<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">National University of Defense Technology</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/peihonglin\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Peihong Lin<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">National University of Defense Technology</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/danjunliu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Danjun Liu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">National University of Defense Technology</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/baoshengwang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Baosheng Wang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">National University of Defense Technology</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/xuzhou\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Xu Zhou<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">National University of Defense Technology</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br><div class=\"row\" style=\"padding:4px 0px;\"><label class=\"col-sm-2 control-label\" style=\"text-align:right;\">AnchorDiff-ICSE-2026</label><div class=\"col-sm-10\"><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-8\"><div clas